{
  "opening": "This release introduces several critical bug fixes and new features to enhance the robustness of string parsing. It addresses issues with numeric type handling, brace matching, and result object usability while adding support for case-sensitive searches and slice access.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The Parser must provide a 'letters' matcher that matches alphabetic characters only, distinct from the 'w' pattern which also matches numbers. Users can utilize this new matcher within their format specifications."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "Result instances must support the `__contains__` method, allowing users to check if a specific value exists within the parsed results. This applies to both Match objects contained in the result and the Result object itself when checking against its contents."
    },
    {
      "id": "m05",
      "text": "The Parser must raise an error or fail to match if a part is not fully enclosed in matching braces. This ensures that malformed brace usage does not silently produce incorrect matches."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "FixedTzOffset must correctly handle timezone offset parsing as per the reported bug fix. The behavior should align with standard expectations for timezone offset representation."
    },
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The Parser must correctly parse Fortran-formatted floating-point numbers. This includes recognizing the specific syntax used in Fortran float representations without raising errors."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17",
      "text": "Hexadecimal numbers specified with type 'x' must be recognized as numeric types internally. The int_convert function must allow the base argument to be optional and automatically detect the base, while correctly identifying signed hexadecimal, decimal, and other integer formats."
    },
    {
      "id": "m21",
      "text": "The convert_first, int_convert, and with_pattern functions must remain functional and picklable after internal refactoring. The public API signatures for these names must remain unchanged and compatible with existing usage."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23",
      "text": "The findall function must respect the case_sensitive parameter when searching for patterns. When case_sensitive is True, it should only return matches that exactly match the case of the pattern."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25",
      "text": "Left- and center-aligned search operations must consume input up to the next space character. This behavior applies across all affected public names including Parser, compile, parse, search, and related conversion functions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28",
      "text": "Result instances must support slice access, allowing users to retrieve subsets of matched values using standard Python slicing syntax. For example, accessing result[0:2] should return the corresponding slice of matched items."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public APIs behave as described above. These changes are essential for maintaining compatibility and correctness in downstream applications."
}
